-- g6-tests-warning.l4: tests of ss.52-54.
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.52-54 (law.wiki lines 395-408; gazette p. 195) and from
-- Interpretation Law s.10 before any run.  The dates:
--   a warning delivered Wednesday 3 March 2027;
--   s.53(a): 30 days from it, IL s.10(a): Friday 2 April 2027; if Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April are days of
--     rest, IL s.10(c) moves the end to Sunday 4 April 2027 (32 days after delivery);
--   the alternative anchor, a breach on Wednesday 10 February 2027: 30 days end on Friday 12 March 2027
--     (11 to 28 February are 18 days, 1 to 12 March 12 more);
--   s.54(b): two years after 3 March 2027 is 3 March 2029, a Saturday (IL s.10(b)); the day of delivery itself is
--     outside the window and the last day is inside.  With Saturday 3 March 2029 a day of rest, IL s.10(c) (the
--     PLAN's kind W, the alternative) moves the end to Sunday 4 March 2029.

§ `Tests of ss 52 to 54`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an individual violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-IND", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`another individual`     MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-OTHER", `kind of person` IS `an individual`

`violation (1)` MEANS `work with no licence at all`
`violation (2)` MEANS `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`
`violation (3)` MEANS `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`

`no day of rest at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY
`Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 4 2), (YMD 2027 4 3)
`Saturday 3 March 2029 as a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2029 3 3)

-- Positional fields of `Administrative warning`: violator, violation the warning concerns, delivered on,
-- states act+date, tells to stop, warns of a sanction, states the right to ask for cancellation, cancelled.
`a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027`   MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a warning that omits the act and its date`                  MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a warning that does not tell the violator to stop`          MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a warning that does not warn of a sanction`                 MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a warning that omits the right to ask for cancellation`     MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a complete warning on item (1) that was cancelled`          MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE

`no extension granted` MEANS NOTHING
`an extension to 10 May 2027 with reasons recorded`    MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 5 10, TRUE)
`an extension to 10 May 2027 without reasons recorded` MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 5 10, FALSE)

GIVEN who IS A Person
      item IS A `Listed violation`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A Violation
`a violation by` who `of` item `on` day MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS who
                 , `the listed violation` IS item
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS day

§§ `s 52(a): the Commissioner may give a warning instead of a sanction (all four conditions)`

#ASSERT     `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give an administrative warning instead of a financial sanction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give an administrative warning instead of a financial sanction` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give an administrative warning instead of a financial sanction` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give an administrative warning instead of a financial sanction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give an administrative warning instead of a financial sanction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

§§ `s 52(b): the warning states what the Law requires`

#ASSERT     `s 52(b) — the administrative warning states what the Law requires` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(b) — the administrative warning states what the Law requires` `a warning that omits the act and its date`
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(b) — the administrative warning states what the Law requires` `a warning that does not tell the violator to stop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(b) — the administrative warning states what the Law requires` `a warning that does not warn of a sanction`
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(b) — the administrative warning states what the Law requires` `a warning that omits the right to ask for cancellation`

-- The power as a MAY guarded by the warning's contents.
#TRACE `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give the violator an administrative warning` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give the violator an administrative warning` `the Commissioner` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` AT 5
#TRACE `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give the violator an administrative warning` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give the violator an administrative warning` `the Commissioner` `a warning that omits the act and its date` AT 5
#TRACE `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give the violator an administrative warning` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

§§ `s 53(a): 30 days, the anchor not stated (F-ANCHOR), IL s.10(a) and IL s.10(c) (kind W)`

#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the last day of the 30 days from` (YMD 2027 3 3) `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the last day of the 30 days from` (YMD 2027 3 3) `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 4
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — without s 10(c), the last day of the 30 days from` (YMD 2027 3 3) EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
-- Counted from the delivery of the warning (taken) and from the day of the breach (the alternative anchor).
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel, counting from the day of the breach` (YMD 2027 2 10) `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 12

-- (b): an extension by the Commissioner, with recorded reasons; without them it is ignored.
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 10 May 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 10
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 10 May 2027 without reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `no extension granted` `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 4

#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the days from the delivery of` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `to the last day to ask to cancel, given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the days from the delivery of` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `to the last day to ask to cancel, given` `no extension granted` `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS 32

-- Both edges of the window (fork F-ACTDAY): a request made ON the day the warning is delivered is "within 30 days" of
-- it; a day before the warning was delivered is not; the last day is inside.
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 3 2) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 3 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- The strict reading, callable: the period starts the day AFTER delivery.
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 3 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 53(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 3 4) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 53(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 4 2) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` (YMD 2027 4 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 3 4) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 4 2) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 4 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT     `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 4 4) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 4 5) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `no extension granted` `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest`

-- The right (a MAY, in writing, on one of the two grounds, within the period).
#TRACE `s 53(a) — the violator may ask for the warning to be cancelled` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `no extension granted` `no day of rest at all` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `ask the Commissioner in writing to cancel the administrative warning` `the violator` TRUE `the violator did not commit the breach` AT 30
-- A request that is not in writing is not the request the section allows: the permission stands.
#TRACE `s 53(a) — the violator may ask for the warning to be cancelled` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `no extension granted` `no day of rest at all` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `ask the Commissioner in writing to cancel the administrative warning` `the violator` FALSE `the act the violator committed, as detailed in the warning, is not a breach` AT 10
-- A warning that was cancelled leaves nothing to cancel.
#TRACE `s 53(a) — the violator may ask for the warning to be cancelled` `a complete warning on item (1) that was cancelled` `no extension granted` `no day of rest at all` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

-- The Commissioner's power to extend, and (c): decide, then give the decision in writing with reasons.
#TRACE `s 53(b) — the Commissioner may extend the period to ask for cancellation` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `extend the period to ask for cancellation of the warning` `the Commissioner` (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 5 10, TRUE) AT 3
#TRACE `s 53(b) — the Commissioner may extend the period to ask for cancellation` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 3)

#ASSERT     `s 53(c) — the decision is in writing and gives reasons` (`Written decision on a request to cancel a warning` OF YMD 2027 3 20, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(c) — the decision is in writing and gives reasons` (`Written decision on a request to cancel a warning` OF YMD 2027 3 20, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(c) — the decision is in writing and gives reasons` (`Written decision on a request to cancel a warning` OF YMD 2027 3 20, TRUE, FALSE)

#TRACE `s 53(c) — the Commissioner decides a request to cancel the warning` TRUE `to cancel the warning` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `decide a request to cancel an administrative warning` `the Commissioner` `to cancel the warning` AT 10
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give the violator the decision on the request in writing with reasons` `the Commissioner` (`Written decision on a request to cancel a warning` OF YMD 2027 3 20, TRUE, TRUE) AT 12
#TRACE `s 53(c) — the Commissioner decides a request to cancel the warning` TRUE `to refuse the request and leave the warning in place` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `decide a request to cancel an administrative warning` `the Commissioner` `to refuse the request and leave the warning in place` AT 10
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give the violator the decision on the request in writing with reasons` `the Commissioner` (`Written decision on a request to cancel a warning` OF YMD 2027 3 20, TRUE, FALSE) AT 12
#TRACE `s 53(c) — the Commissioner decides a request to cancel the warning` FALSE `to cancel the warning` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

§§ `s 54(a): a breach that continues after a warning is a continuing violation`

#ASSERT     `s 54(a) — a breach continued after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (1)` `and the violator having continued:` TRUE
-- Items (1) and (2) both contravene s.3(a): a continued item (2) breach after an item (1) warning is the same provision.
#ASSERT     `s 54(a) — a breach continued after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (2)` `and the violator having continued:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(a) — a breach continued after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (3)` `and the violator having continued:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(a) — a breach continued after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (1)` `and the violator having continued:` FALSE
-- A cancelled warning (F-CANCEL): nothing follows (taken); the alternative ignores the cancellation.
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(a) — a breach continued after` `a complete warning on item (1) that was cancelled` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (1)` `and the violator having continued:` TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 54(a) — ignoring any cancellation, a breach continued after` `a complete warning on item (1) that was cancelled` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (1)` `and the violator having continued:` TRUE

-- The months (F-START): from the day the breach began (10 February 2027) or from the delivery of the warning (3 March).
-- Until 2 June 2027: counted from 10 February, month 1 ends on 10 March, month 2 on 10 April, month 3 on 10 May and
-- month 4 would end on 10 June, after the 2nd: 3 months.  Counted from 3 March, month 1 ends on 3 April, month 2 on
-- 3 May and month 3 would end on 3 June: 2 months.
#ASSERT `s 54(a) — the months of a continuing violation counted from the day the breach began` (YMD 2027 2 10) `until` (YMD 2027 6 2) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 54(a) — the months of a continuing violation counted from the delivery of` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `until` (YMD 2027 6 2) EQUALS 2

§§ `s 54(b): a further breach within two years of the delivery of the warning is a repeat violation (kind B)`

#ASSERT `s 54(b) — the last day of the two years from the delivery of` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` EQUALS YMD 2029 3 3
-- Both edges: the day of delivery is outside, the next day is inside, the last day is inside, the day after is outside.
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 3))
#ASSERT     `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 4))
#ASSERT     `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 3))
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 4))
-- The same provision (items (1) and (2) both s.3(a)), the same violator, a warning not cancelled.
#ASSERT     `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (2)` `on` (YMD 2028 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (3)` `on` (YMD 2028 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `another individual` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) that was cancelled` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 1 1))
-- With IL s.10(c) applied (F-WINDOW-54): 3 March 2029 a day of rest moves the end to Sunday 4 March 2029.
#ASSERT `s 54(b) — the last day of the two years from the delivery of` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `, when s 10(c) applies, with` `Saturday 3 March 2029 as a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2029 3 4
#ASSERT     `s 54(b) — with s 10(c) applied to the window, the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 4)) `, with` `Saturday 3 March 2029 as a day of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 54(b) — with s 10(c) applied to the window, the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 5)) `, with` `Saturday 3 March 2029 as a day of rest`

-- The Commissioner's duty after a warning: a MUST to give a notice of intention that states what s.42(b) requires.
-- Positional fields of `Notice of intention`: delivered on, in writing, act+date, amount, period (days), right, deemed
-- demand, power to add, intention to publish name.
`a complete notice of intention` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2027 9 1, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST 30, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a notice of intention that omits the amount` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2027 9 1, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, JUST 30, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#TRACE `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction after a warning` `the Commissioner` `a complete notice of intention` AT 20
#TRACE `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction after a warning` `the Commissioner` `a notice of intention that omits the amount` AT 20
#TRACE `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 50)
-- F-MUST54: the alternative keeps s.42(a)'s condition, so a Commissioner who does not intend to impose is not bound.
#TRACE `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning, if he intends to impose a sanction` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 50)
#TRACE `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning, if he intends to impose a sanction` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 50)

§§ `Trap T17: "repeat violation" in s 45(b) and in s 54(b) is anchored differently (the discriminating cases)`

-- Positional fields of `Previous violation`: violator, violation, date of the act, sanction imposed, convicted.
`a sanctioned item (1) violation on 10 January 2027` MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 1 10, TRUE, FALSE
`an item (1) violation on 10 January 2027 that ended in a warning only` MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 1 10, FALSE, FALSE

-- A further item (1) violation on 20 February 2029.
--   s.45(b): the window from the sanctioned violation of 10 January 2027 ended on 10 January 2029, so it is NOT a repeat.
--   s.54(b): the warning of 3 March 2027 gives a window to 3 March 2029, so it IS a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 2 20)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `a sanctioned item (1) violation on 10 January 2027`)
#ASSERT     `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 2 20))
-- A violation that ended in a warning only is no "previous violation for which a sanction was imposed or a conviction
-- obtained", so s.45(b) alone does not make a further violation a repeat; s.54(b) deems it one.
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an item (1) violation on 10 January 2027 that ended in a warning only`)
#ASSERT     `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1))
-- And on 10 January 2029 itself the two windows agree on the first (last day inside) and differ the day after.
#ASSERT     `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 1 10)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `a sanctioned item (1) violation on 10 January 2027`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 1 11)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `a sanctioned item (1) violation on 10 January 2027`)
#ASSERT     `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 1 11))

§§ `Fork F-SHORTEN: an "extension" that ends before the 30 days are out does not shorten them (s.53(b))`

`an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded`    MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 3 20, TRUE)
`an extension to 20 March 2027 without reasons recorded` MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 3 20, FALSE)
`an extension to Saturday 3 April 2027 with reasons recorded` MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 4 3, TRUE)

#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 without reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
-- With 2 and 3 April days of rest the 30 days end on Sunday 4 April, so an extension to Saturday 3 April is earlier than them.
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to Saturday 3 April 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 4
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the days from the delivery of` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `to the last day to ask to cancel, given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 3 25) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 4 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- The alternative, callable: an extension is the end whatever day it is.
#ASSERT `s 53(b) — taking an extension that ends before the 30 days as it is, the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 20
#ASSERT `s 53(b) — taking an extension that ends before the 30 days as it is, the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 without reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 53(b) — taking an extension that ends before the 30 days as it is, the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `no extension granted` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
#ASSERT `s 53(b) — taking an extension that ends before the 30 days as it is, the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 10 May 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 10
-- The right lasts the 30 days: the request at the thirtieth day is permitted.
#TRACE `s 53(a) — the violator may ask for the warning to be cancelled` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `no day of rest at all` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `ask the Commissioner in writing to cancel the administrative warning` `the violator` TRUE `the violator did not commit the breach` AT 30
